  "result": "I found the bug and wrote up a plan, but I haven't changed any code because plan mode is active. I couldn't call ExitPlanMode (it's disabled in this session), so please approve the plan here and I'll make the change.\n\n**Cause:** `IntRange._clamp` in `src/click/types.py:754` returns `bound - dir`, which moves away from the valid range. `convert` passes `dir=1` for the minimum and `dir=-1` for the maximum, so the sign is backwards. With an open bound and `clamp=True`:\n- `IntRange(min=0, min_open=True, clamp=True)` turns `-5` into `-1` instead of `1`.\n- `IntRange(max=10, max_open=True, clamp=True)` turns `20` into `11` instead of `9`.\n\n**Fix:** change `return bound - dir` to `return bound + dir`. `FloatRange` isn't affected, because it rejects clamping with open bounds.\n\n**Tests:** I'd add regression cases to `tests/test_types.py` for both open-bound examples above, then run `pytest tests/test_types.py tests/test_info_dict.py`.\n\nThe plan is saved at `<home>\\.claude\\plans\\some-users-report-that-elegant-thacker.md`.",
